All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress loop took 3.0s). I ran the suite after each function; `test_impl.py` is untouched.

- **`encode`** (`rle.py`): groups consecutive characters and emits each character followed by its run length.
- **`decode`** (`rle.py`): reads each non-digit character plus the digits after it and expands the run.
- **`merge`** (`intervals.py`): sorts by start, then extends the last interval whenever the next one starts at or before its end, so touching intervals merge.

The format itself can't round-trip strings that contain digits: `encode("1")` gives `"11"`, which `decode` can't read back. The docstrings and tests don't cover that case, so I left it alone.

Changes are uncommitted, and running the tests left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
